---
import '../../src/index.css'
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="reachq is a Python library for exact reachability shortcut sets and weighted shortest-path hopsets on directed graphs." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/reachq/favicon.svg" />
    <title>reachq — Graph reachability, queryable.</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="shell nav-wrap">
        <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="reachq home"><img class="brand-lockup" src="/reachq/logo-reversed.svg" alt="reachq" /></a>
        <button class="menu-toggle" aria-label="Open navigation" aria-expanded="false">Menu</button>
        <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="#status">Status</a><a href="#product">What it does</a><a href="#workflow">How it works</a><a href="#docs">Docs</a>
        </nav>
        <div class="nav-actions"><a class="nav-github" href="https://github.com/sachncs/reachq" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a><a class="button button-small" href="/reachq/getting-started.html">Get started <span>→</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="top">
      <section class="hero shell">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Graph algorithms for Python</div>
          <h1>Graph reachability,<br /><em>queryable.</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-lede">reachq is a focused Python library for building exact reachability shortcut sets and weighted shortest-path hopsets on directed graphs. It makes the construction, query, and verification steps explicit.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/reachq/getting-started.html">Start with the docs <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/sachncs/reachq" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the source <span>↗</span></a></div>
          <div class="trust-row"><span>MIT licensed</span><span>Python 3.10–3.13</span><span>Pre-1.0</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-visual">
          <div class="visual-glow"></div><div class="visual-topline"><span>REACHQ / QUERY PATH</span><span class="live"><i></i> explicit</span></div>
          <svg class="graph-art" viewBox="0 0 560 460" role="img" aria-label="Directed graph with a highlighted query path"><defs><linearGradient id="line" x1="0" x2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#4d5b6e" stop-opacity=".2"></stop><stop offset=".5" stop-color="#b8ff65"></stop><stop offset="1" stop-color="#69e0ff" stop-opacity=".45"></stop></linearGradient></defs><g class="graph-lines"><path d="M54 322 L144 150 L248 260 L340 106 L458 190 L520 80"></path><path d="M54 322 L184 382 L248 260 L366 356 L458 190"></path><path d="M144 150 L340 106 L366 356"></path><path d="M248 260 L458 190 L520 80"></path><path d="M184 382 L366 356 L520 80"></path></g><path class="query-line" d="M54 322 L144 150 L248 260 L340 106 L458 190 L520 80"></path><g class="graph-nodes"><circle cx="54" cy="322" r="10"></circle><circle cx="144" cy="150" r="7"></circle><circle cx="184" cy="382" r="7"></circle><circle cx="248" cy="260" r="12"></circle><circle cx="340" cy="106" r="8"></circle><circle cx="366" cy="356" r="8"></circle><circle cx="458" cy="190" r="11"></circle><circle cx="520" cy="80" r="8"></circle></g><circle class="pulse" cx="248" cy="260" r="21"></circle><circle class="pulse pulse-delay" cx="458" cy="190" r="19"></circle></svg>
          <div class="visual-footer"><span>G + H</span><span>•</span><span>verify the invariant</span><span class="visual-bound">seed <strong>42</strong></span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="status-strip" id="status"><div class="shell status-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">Project status</div><h2>Pre-1.0, source-first, research-aware.</h2><p>The core API is usable and tested, but compatibility is not promised before 1.0. Install from a source checkout and read the explicit limits before adoption.</p></div><div class="status-meta"><span class="status-badge"><i></i> Active development</span><span>0.9.0.dev0</span><span>Pure-Python core</span><span>No PyPI release yet</span></div></div></section>

      <section class="section onboarding-section" id="install"><div class="shell onboarding-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / Install</div><h2>Start from a clean<br /><span>source checkout.</span></h2><p>Keeping the code, tests, examples, and docs on one commit makes the current behavior inspectable.</p></div><div><div class="install-command"><span>$</span> git clone https://github.com/sachncs/reachq && cd reachq && pip install -e ".[dev]" <button aria-label="Copy install command">⧉</button></div><div class="install-notes"><span>Python 3.10–3.13</span><span>NumPy ≥ 1.21</span><span>SciPy ≥ 1.10</span></div></div></div></section>

      <section class="section example-section" id="quickstart"><div class="shell"><div class="example-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / Minimal working example</div><h2>Build a shortcut set.<br /><span>Then prove it.</span></h2></div><p>The first example does not promise a speedup. It constructs a result, checks exact reachability preservation, and makes the realized bound visible.</p></div><div class="example-layout"><div class="example-notes"><div><strong>Input</strong><span>A deterministic directed graph.</span></div><div><strong>Construction</strong><span>Shortcuts plus beta and realised bound.</span></div><div><strong>Invariant</strong><span>Original and augmented reachability agree.</span></div></div><pre class="example-window"><code><span class="code-purple">from</span> reachq.generators <span class="code-purple">import</span> random_dag
<span class="code-purple">from</span> reachq.shortcut <span class="code-purple">import</span> build_shortcut_set_for_reachability
<span class="code-purple">from</span> reachq.invariants <span class="code-purple">import</span> assert_reachability_preserved

graph = random_dag(n=<span class="code-green">100</span>, edge_probability=<span class="code-green">0.1</span>, random_seed=<span class="code-green">42</span>)
shortcuts, beta, realised_bound = build_shortcut_set_for_reachability(
    graph, omega=<span class="code-green">3.0</span>, random_seed=<span class="code-green">42</span>
)
assert_reachability_preserved(graph, shortcuts)</code></pre></div></div></section>

      <section class="section why-section" id="product"><div class="shell why-grid"><div class="why-heading"><div class="eyebrow">What reachq does</div><h2>Two constructions.<br /><span>One clear boundary.</span></h2><p>Use reachq when the graph algorithm itself is the work: precompute structure, run a bounded query, and check the result against an explicit invariant.</p></div><div class="why-list"><article><span class="why-number">01</span><div><h3>Shortcut sets for reachability</h3><p>Add directed edges while preserving which vertices are reachable from each source.</p></div></article><article><span class="why-number">02</span><div><h3>Hopsets for weighted paths</h3><p>Add weighted links and query with a hop limit while keeping epsilon visible.</p></div></article><article><span class="why-number">03</span><div><h3>Checks close to the code</h3><p>Seeds, bounds, serialization, and invariants make algorithmic experiments inspectable.</p></div></article></div></div></section>

      <section class="section architecture-section" id="workflow"><div class="shell"><div class="architecture-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">03 / How it works</div><h2>Construct once.<br /><span>Measure what follows.</span></h2></div><p>The library separates construction from querying so you can compare setup cost, query cost, memory, and correctness on your own graph family.</p></div><div class="architecture-grid"><article class="architecture-card"><div class="architecture-tag">Exact relation</div><h3>Shortcut sets</h3><p>Build <code>H</code>, query <code>G ∪ H</code>, and verify that reachability is unchanged.</p><div class="architecture-flow"><span>G</span><b>+</b><span>H</span><b>→</b><strong>same reachability</strong></div><a href="/reachq/concepts/shortcut-sets.html">Read the concept <span>→</span></a></article><article class="architecture-card architecture-card-accent"><div class="architecture-tag">Bounded query</div><h3>Hopsets</h3><p>Build weighted links, query with <code>max_hops</code>, and compare distances with exact Dijkstra.</p><div class="architecture-flow"><span>G</span><b>+</b><span>H<sub>w</sub></span><b>→</b><strong>epsilon is explicit</strong></div><a href="/reachq/concepts/hopsets.html">Read the concept <span>→</span></a></article></div></div></section>

      <section class="section guarantees-section"><div class="shell"><div class="guarantees-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">04 / Read the contract</div><h2>Useful because<br /><span>the limits are visible.</span></h2></div><p>Formal results, implementation behavior, and measured performance are different kinds of evidence. The docs keep them separate.</p></div><div class="guarantees-grid"><article><span class="guarantee-icon">✓</span><h3>Exact preservation</h3><p>Shortcut workflows expose an invariant for the reachable relation.</p></article><article><span class="guarantee-icon">≈</span><h3>Explicit epsilon</h3><p>Hopset checks compare bounded paths with an exact baseline.</p></article><article><span class="guarantee-icon">↺</span><h3>Seeded runs</h3><p>Insertion order and random seeds support reproducible experiments.</p></article><article><span class="guarantee-icon">!</span><h3>Visible limits</h3><p>No blanket speedup, hosted service, or pre-1.0 compatibility promise.</p></article></div></div></section>

      <section class="section docs-section" id="docs"><div class="shell"><div class="docs-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">05 / Documentation</div><h2>Start with the concept.<br /><span>Then inspect the implementation.</span></h2></div><p>The docs are organized by the question you are trying to answer: install, understand, build, reference, research, or contribute.</p></div><div class="docs-grid"><a href="/reachq/getting-started.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">01</span><h3>Getting started</h3><p>Install and run the first verified construction.</p><span class="doc-link">Start here →</span></a><a href="/reachq/reference.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">02</span><h3>API reference</h3><p>Find the supported graph, query, configuration, and invariant surface.</p><span class="doc-link">Browse API →</span></a><a href="/reachq/algorithms.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">03</span><h3>Concepts</h3><p>Understand shortcut sets, hopsets, correctness, and limitations.</p><span class="doc-link">Understand the model →</span></a><a href="/reachq/benchmarks.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">04</span><h3>Benchmarks</h3><p>Record the context needed to make a result reproducible.</p><span class="doc-link">Measure honestly →</span></a><a href="/reachq/research/provenance.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">05</span><h3>Research</h3><p>Separate paper provenance from current implementation behavior.</p><span class="doc-link">Read the boundary →</span></a><a href="/reachq/project/contributing.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">06</span><h3>Contributing</h3><p>Set up the project and make changes that stay maintainable.</p><span class="doc-link">Join the work →</span></a></div></div></section>

      <section class="section research-section"><div class="shell research-panel"><div class="research-copy"><div class="eyebrow">06 / Provenance</div><h2>Research depth,<br /><span>product clarity.</span></h2><p>The constructions are informed by published graph-algorithm research. reachq keeps literature results, implementation facts, and benchmark observations distinct.</p><a class="button button-dark" href="/reachq/research/provenance.html">Read the provenance <span>→</span></a></div><div class="research-stats"><div><strong>0.9</strong><span>development snapshot</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>core constructions</span></div><div><strong>1</strong><span>explicit boundary</span></div></div></div></section>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer"><div class="shell footer-wrap"><a class="brand" href="#top"><img class="brand-lockup" src="/reachq/logo-reversed.svg" alt="reachq" /></a><span>Graph reachability, queryable.</span><div><a href="https://github.com/sachncs/reachq" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a><a href="/reachq/project/contributing.html">Contribute ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/sachncs/reachq/blob/master/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MIT License</a></div></div></footer>
    <script type="module">
      const menu = document.querySelector('.menu-toggle')
      const nav = document.querySelector('.nav-links')
      menu?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const open = nav?.classList.toggle('nav-open')
        menu.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open))
      })
      document.querySelector('[aria-label="Copy install command"]')?.addEventListener('click', async (event) => {
        await navigator.clipboard?.writeText('git clone https://github.com/sachncs/reachq && cd reachq && pip install -e ".[dev]"')
        event.currentTarget.textContent = '✓'
      })
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
